  "description": "The meme is designed for a broad general audience, particularly those familiar with the gluten-free diet trend and the cultural discourse surrounding gluten allergies. It targets individuals who may be skeptical of gluten-related health claims, or who are aware of the trend but not fully informed about the medical distinctions between celiac disease, non-celiac gluten sensitivity, and gluten-free fads. The humor relies on the contrast between historical bread consumption and the modern perception of gluten as a widespread allergen, appealing to those who understand or have encountered the gluten-free movement in popular culture.",
